.TH SWL 1 "2026-07-27" "swl 2.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
swl \- real-time log anomaly detection with contextual debugging
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swl
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ LOGFILE ]
.br
.B swl
.I SUBCOMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B swl
watches log files 24/7 for anomalies. When something goes wrong, it captures
the surrounding context and optionally sends alerts to Slack, Discord, or any
webhook endpoint.
.PP
Unlike simple grep-based tools,
.B swl
maintains a sliding window of recent lines and captures both pre-context (before
the trigger) and post-context (after the trigger), giving you the full picture
of what happened.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.SS Monitoring
.TP
.BI \-\-log " PATH"
Log file to monitor. Auto-discovered if omitted.
.TP
.BI \-\-webhook " URL"
Webhook URL for alerts (Slack, Discord, etc.). Omit for local-only logging.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Path to config file. Auto-loaded from standard locations.
.TP
.BI \-\-triggers " K1,K2,..."
Comma-separated keywords or regex patterns. Default: \fBFATAL,ERROR\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " E1,E2,..."
Exclusion patterns. Lines matching these are skipped.
.TP
.BI \-\-window " N"
Lines to keep in context buffer. Default: \fB100\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-trailing " N"
Lines to capture after trigger. Default: \fB20\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-incidents " DIR"
Directory for incident reports. Default: \fB/var/log/swl-incidents\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-cooldown " SEC"
Minimum seconds between alerts per trigger. Default: \fB60\fR.
.SS Webhook
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " N"
Max webhook retry attempts. Default: \fB3\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-retry\-delay " MS"
Delay between retries in milliseconds. Default: \fB1000\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ssl\-verify
Disable SSL certificate verification (for self-signed certs).
.SS Security
.TP
.BI \-\-user " USER"
Drop to this user after opening log (requires root).
.TP
.BI \-\-pid\-file " PATH"
PID file for stop/clean commands. Default: \fB.swl.pid\fR.
.SS Limits
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-line\-length " N"
Maximum characters per log line. Default: \fB8192\fR.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B swl init
Generate config file in current directory.
.TP
.B swl status
Print current config and runtime information.
.TP
.B swl incidents
List recent incident reports.
.TP
.B swl logs
Follow latest incident file.
.TP
.B swl stop
Stop a running instance.
.TP
.B swl clean
Stop and remove generated files.
.SH CONFIGURATION
swl loads configuration from the first file found in:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
/etc/swl/config
~/.config/swl/config
./.swl.conf
.fi
.RE
.PP
Config file format:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
log = /var/log/app.log
webhook = https://hooks.slack.com/services/xxx
triggers = FATAL,ERROR,WARN
excludes = DEBUG,healthcheck
window = 100
trailing = 20
cooldown = 60
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Monitor syslog:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
swl /var/log/syslog
.fi
.RE
.PP
Monitor with webhook alerts:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
swl \-\-webhook https://hooks.slack.com/services/xxx /var/log/app.log
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate and edit config:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
swl init
vim .swl.conf
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check status:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
swl status
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/swl/config
System config file (highest priority in production).
.TP
.B ~/.config/swl/config
User config file.
.TP
.B ./.swl.conf
Local config file (development).
.TP
.B ./.swl.pid
PID file for running instance.
.TP
.B /var/log/swl-incidents/
Directory for incident reports.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (or help/version displayed).
.TP
.B 1
Error (invalid arguments, file not found, etc.).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to find user config directory.
